      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Setting the render distance on the fly is something I can totally agree with. It would help a lot on older hardware. For the other stuff, well I wouldn't need it but if it's there people would use it for sure. Many worlds overdo it a bit when it comes to post FX for example so turning them off on the fly or tweaking them would be nice, the same goes for real-time shadows. If possible it should not be a simple on off toggle but more like sliders to select the number of pixel lights or the amount of post processing. Great request, indeed.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-11-06T16:22:08.292Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Issue: VRChat is consistently one of the longest \"duration of use\" vr applications on the market, with players often spending 3,5, even 12 hours wearing a headset with few breaks.\nSome, (but not all), headsets manufacturers offer a \"night mode\". However, that's is where the options typically end, without third party add-ons like OpenVR Advanced settings. \n\nOne other social application, \"Bigscreen VR\" offers many visual enhancements and adjustments for end users. \n\nOne example option would be the ability to completely force disable post processing if a world is using it.\n\nAnother would be the ability to manually set distance culling in an attempt to improve performance.\n\nAnother would be the ability to disable real-time shadows and reflections on dynamic objects when needed, as this is a major cost to performance.\n\nAnother would be to toggle on monoscopic rendering, as some shaders and filters can cause a \"one blinking eye\" effect for many vr users.\n\nI have a world that does this by accident for quest (but not pc) users, for example. \n\nFinally, very recently an asset was released called DiCE: Dichoptic Contrast Enhancement. \n\nThis provides increased contrast for the vr user with nearly no cost to rendering, and would be an excellent \"visual filter\" in vrchat's options, that would bring up the perceived visual quality of vrchat compared to other applications. \n\nhttps://assetstore.unity.com/packages/tools/particles-effects/dice-dichoptic-contrast-enhancement-for-vr-and-stereo-displays-155141",
